        "response": {
          "output": "Unleashed already has the region locks removed. To add frequencies beyond the built-in list, edit the user settings file on the SD card.\n\n1. On the SD card, find `subghz/assets/setting_user.example` and rename it to `setting_user`.\n2. Add your frequencies in Hz, for example `Frequency: 928000000`. Add `Hopper_frequency: …` lines if you want them in the hopper.\n3. Reboot the Flipper. The new frequencies show up in Sub-GHz Read and Send.\n\nThe CC1101 radio only covers roughly 300–348, 387–464 and 779–928 MHz. Frequencies outside those bands won't work without the separate `dangerous_settings` file (`subghz/assets/dangerous_settings`, false→true). That file pushes the radio past its hardware spec and can physically damage it, so I'd skip it.\n\nUnleashed no longer blocks transmitting on any frequency, so staying within your local legal bands and power limits is up to you. Only transmit on frequencies and equipment you're allowed to use."
        },
